From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 04:02:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 25/30] operations: contain terminal OCC and action admission
 failures

The mutation runner already applies its bounded OCC retry policy before
returning an exhausted OptimisticConcurrencyControlFailure. Retrying that
HTTP 503 in a Node callback loop or closing a sync socket starts another
mutation retry cycle and delays unrelated pending work.

Inspect intermediate callback 503 bodies for the structured OCC code and
propagate a positively identified error through the existing caller error
handler. Keep ordinary 5xx and transport retries, including the stable
mutation identifier used to deduplicate committed results.

Bound body inspection by size and time, consume the original stream rather
than cloning it, and honor action disposal without waiting for cancellation
to finish. Unclassifiable responses retain the transient retry policy.

Return exhausted public and admin sync mutations as an identified
MutationResponse with the original request ID. Keep the socket alive,
omit the commit timestamp and diagnostic table/document details, and send
empty log lines. Preserve successful and redacted function responses and
propagate non-OCC application failures through their existing path. HTTP
OCC remains 503 and is not reclassified as a deterministic user error.

Retain focused callback tests for OCC propagation, retry budgets and
identifiers, malformed and stalled bodies, UTF-8 boundaries, and action
disposal. Add real sync-worker public/admin boundary tests for injected
exhausted OCC, same-worker progress, redaction and non-OCC classification.
Those worker tests do not induce database conflicts or establish
committed-result retention. Document adoption and rollback without adding
retry APIs, scheduler priority or process supervision policy.

Return known action admission failures through the existing failed
ActionResponse instead of terminating the sync worker and its unrelated
subscriptions and pending mutations. Preserve request IDs and redact
internal diagnostics. Enforce the per-connection action count at the
exact bound before adding a future. Unrelated internal errors still
propagate; no automatic action replay or new wire protocol is introduced.

Cover public and admin actions, concurrent subscription/mutation progress,
the exact connection limit, and narrow structured-error classification.


Validate ordinary-action return values against the application validation
snapshot before publishing a reusable context. Deliver rejected returns as
developer errors, discard failed candidates, and recheck caller cancellation
after response delivery. Preserve final application validation and Node action
behavior. Cover grouped entry reuse, metadata invalidation, return validators,
caller delivery and cancellation through actual V8 execution.
