+## Operation error propagation
+
+### [Request-local operation failures](terminal_occ/README.md)
+
+- Purpose: return exhausted per-mutation optimistic concurrency control (OCC) to its caller without
+  restarting the mutation retry budget in a Node callback loop or by closing its sync socket;
+  return known action admission failures to their request without disconnecting unrelated work.
+- Prerequisites: the existing application mutation runner and Node callback retry loop; no scheduler,
+  priority, or native-resident supervision changes.
+- Activation: automatic for identified exhausted OCC and action admission failures; no new
+  configuration, wire message, or action retry.
+- Rollback: restore the previous backend and Node executor together; exhausted sync mutations
+  and rejected sync actions can close the socket again, and exhausted callback mutations can
+  receive additional retry cycles.
